{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure wg01 on node1 and node2 as a routed WireGuard tunnel connecting lan-a and lan-b.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"No WireGuard configuration, handshake, route, or cross-LAN connectivity evidence was captured. The gateway baseline predates execution, while both final gateway observations were unavailable after the cluster lease expired.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","global:before_prepare:node2:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node2:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Keep traffic routed through the tunnel free of address translation.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"There is no NAT configuration inspection, packet capture, connection tracking output, or source-address observation from cross-LAN traffic.","evidence_ids":[]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Serve the lan-a application from node3 on TCP port 8080 and make it reachable from node4 through the tunnel.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The baseline socket inventory shows no TCP/8080 listener on node3, but it is not a final observation. Final node3 and node4 state was unavailable, and no node4-to-node3 application request was captured.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node3:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node3:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node4:platform"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Permit new cross-LAN connections only for the node4-to-node3 TCP/8080 application path.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"No firewall-policy inspection or bounded positive and negative connection tests were captured, so the required restriction cannot be assessed.","evidence_ids":["global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.05,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"The complete executor timeline contains no commands, so no state-changing actions or unnecessary mutations were observed; consequently, there are no unnecessary mutations to identify as retained or reverted. Baseline services and package state were healthy, but final residue, failed services, exposure, and package health could not be inspected because every after-executor observation was unavailable. That uncertainty lowers confidence rather than demonstrating an executor-caused hygiene defect.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:before_prepare:node2:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node2:package-health","global:before_prepare:node3:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node3:package-health","global:before_prepare:node4:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node4:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"None of the four material task outcomes can be verified. There was no captured executor activity or selected task evidence, and all after-executor observations failed because the managed-cluster lease had expired. The baseline alone cannot establish final task state.","limitations":["The executor final report was unavailable, and the captured executor command timeline was empty.","All after-executor observations on node1 through node4 were unavailable because the managed-cluster lease expired; apparent removed lines in the comparison therefore represent unavailable observations, not demonstrated state removal.","The provider-wide restart protocol was not captured for any managed node. Although pre-restart boot identities exist, there are no restart acknowledgements, different post-restart boot identities, or observations of recovered service, data, and cluster state.","No direct evidence was captured for WireGuard configuration or handshakes, routed connectivity, NAT absence, TCP/8080 application behavior, or allowed-versus-denied cross-LAN connections."]}
